---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
const title = "Poola Contributors - Founder-led and built in the open";
const description = "Poola is founder-led today and designed to become contributor-powered through open trust language, templates, tooling, design resources and community pilots.";
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} htmlClass="contributors-shell">
  <section class="contrib-hero">
    <div class="container contrib-hero__grid">
      <div class="contrib-hero__copy" data-reveal>
        <p class="signal"><span></span> Founder & contributors</p>
        <h1>Build the trust layer in public.</h1>
        <p class="hero__sub">Poola is founder-led today, but the useful parts of the system should become contributor-powered: trust language, campaign templates, open widgets, local playbooks and AI workflows people can inspect.</p>
        <div class="hero-actions">
          <a class="btn btn--primary" href="#workboard" data-magnetic>Open workboard</a>
          <a class="btn btn--ghost btn--on-dark" href="#open-boundaries">What opens first</a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <aside class="contrib-console" data-reveal="right" aria-label="Poola public contributor workbench">
        <div class="contrib-console__bar">
          <span></span><span></span><span></span>
          <strong>poola/contributors</strong>
        </div>
        <div class="contrib-console__body">
          <div class="contrib-command">
            <span>$</span>
            <code>poola.open("trust-layer")</code>
          </div>
          <div class="contrib-pulse">
            <b>Founder-led</b>
            <i></i>
            <b>Contributor-ready</b>
            <i></i>
            <b>Trust-first</b>
          </div>
          <div class="contrib-queue">
            <article>
              <span>good first Pool</span>
              <strong>Campaign template review</strong>
            </article>
            <article>
              <span>help wanted</span>
              <strong>Trust status language</strong>
            </article>
            <article>
              <span>design track</span>
              <strong>Public Pool proof patterns</strong>
            </article>
          </div>
        </div>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="contrib-principles section--tight" aria-label="Contributor principles">
    <div class="container contrib-principles__inner" data-reveal-group>
      <span data-reveal>Public work beats vague team claims.</span>
      <span data-reveal>Non-code contributions count.</span>
      <span data-reveal>Trust needs boundaries.</span>
      <span data-reveal>Decisions need a trail.</span>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section contrib-workboard" id="workboard">
    <div class="container contrib-workboard__grid">
      <div class="contrib-section-copy" data-reveal>
        <p class="eyebrow">Contributor workboard</p>
        <h2>Clear tracks, not a fake team page.</h2>
        <p class="lead">Strong open-source projects make the next useful action obvious. Poola can do the same by showing where help is wanted, what review looks like and what belongs in the protected core.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="contrib-track-stack" data-reveal-group>
        <details class="contrib-track" open data-reveal>
          <summary><span>01</span><strong>Trust language</strong><em>Review path</em></summary>
          <p>Define status labels, evidence prompts, reporting language and completion wording that make trust visible without pretending risk disappears.</p>
        </details>
        <details class="contrib-track" data-reveal>
          <summary><span>02</span><strong>Pool templates</strong><em>Good first Pool</em></summary>
          <p>Write starter structures for social good, creators, startups, local action, urgent response and community resource drives.</p>
        </details>
        <details class="contrib-track" data-reveal>
          <summary><span>03</span><strong>Open widgets</strong><em>Builder track</em></summary>
          <p>Prototype embeddable Pool surfaces for publishers, partners and communities where people need a trusted next action.</p>
        </details>
        <details class="contrib-track" data-reveal>
          <summary><span>04</span><strong>Design resources</strong><em>Design track</em></summary>
          <p>Create campaign kits, proof patterns, Store files, contribution states and Pool page components that non-developers can reuse.</p>
        </details>
        <details class="contrib-track" data-reveal>
          <summary><span>05</span><strong>Local pilots</strong><em>Community track</em></summary>
          <p>Test real Pools with founders, nonprofits, creators and local groups so the product learns from actual contribution behavior.</p>
        </details>
        <details class="contrib-track" data-reveal>
          <summary><span>06</span><strong>AI workflows</strong><em>Prototype track</em></summary>
          <p>Shape prompts, review checklists and intent-to-Pool flows that help people start better campaigns from conversation.</p>
        </details>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section contrib-artifacts">
    <div class="container section-head center" data-reveal>
      <p class="eyebrow eyebrow--center">Open project signals</p>
      <h2>The page should feel like a project you can enter.</h2>
      <p class="lead">Before Poola asks people to contribute, the project should publish the artifacts that healthy contributor communities expect.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="container artifact-grid" data-reveal-group>
      <article data-reveal>
        <span>01</span>
        <h3>README</h3>
        <p>What Poola is, why it exists, what is ready and where contributors should start.</p>
        <b>Draft first</b>
      </article>
      <article data-reveal>
        <span>02</span>
        <h3>CONTRIBUTING</h3>
        <p>Contribution types, review expectations, response times and what counts as useful work.</p>
        <b>Needed before launch</b>
      </article>
      <article data-reveal>
        <span>03</span>
        <h3>Code of conduct</h3>
        <p>Community standards, private reporting paths and the line between debate and harm.</p>
        <b>Trust requirement</b>
      </article>
      <article data-reveal>
        <span>04</span>
        <h3>Decision log</h3>
        <p>Why major product, safety and open-source decisions were made, not just what changed.</p>
        <b>Public trail</b>
      </article>
      <article data-reveal>
        <span>05</span>
        <h3>Issue labels</h3>
        <p>Clear lanes like good first Pool, help wanted, design review, safety review and protected core.</p>
        <b>Low-friction entry</b>
      </article>
      <article data-reveal>
        <span>06</span>
        <h3>Contributor notes</h3>
        <p>Short public updates that show what changed, who helped and what needs attention next.</p>
        <b>Recognition loop</b>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section contrib-boundaries" id="open-boundaries">
    <div class="container contrib-boundaries__grid">
      <div class="contrib-section-copy" data-reveal>
        <p class="eyebrow">Open, but careful</p>
        <h2>Poola should open the commons, not the attack surface.</h2>
        <p class="lead">The strongest contributor-led products are clear about governance and safety. Poola can be open where openness increases trust, while protecting payments, fraud response and private user data.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="boundary-board" data-reveal-group>
        <article data-reveal>
          <span>Open first</span>
          <h3>Language, templates, schemas</h3>
          <p>Trust statuses, contribution types, campaign playbooks, public docs and partner embed specs.</p>
        </article>
        <article data-reveal>
          <span>Open with review</span>
          <h3>Widgets, design kits, AI prompts</h3>
          <p>Useful shared tooling that needs quality review, accessibility review and security review before public release.</p>
        </article>
        <article data-reveal>
          <span>Protected core</span>
          <h3>Payments, abuse, private data</h3>
          <p>Money movement, fraud logic, moderation queues, reports and sensitive account data stay controlled.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section contrib-pathway">
    <div class="container section-head center" data-reveal>
      <p class="eyebrow eyebrow--center">Contributor pathway</p>
      <h2>From curious person to trusted contributor.</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="container pathway-line" data-reveal-group>
      <article data-reveal><span>Read</span><p>Understand the mission, scope and open boundaries.</p></article>
      <article data-reveal><span>Start small</span><p>Suggest a template, wording fix, research note or design improvement.</p></article>
      <article data-reveal><span>Review together</span><p>Discuss tradeoffs in public and keep sensitive issues private.</p></article>
      <article data-reveal><span>Recognise work</span><p>Credit contributors in notes, releases, docs and community updates.</p></article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section contrib-maker-store" id="spread-the-word">
    <div class="container contrib-maker-store__head" data-reveal>
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Spread the word</p>
        <h2>Contribute by making Poola visible.</h2>
      </div>
      <p class="lead">Not every contribution is code. Supporters can print, wear, share, host and carry Poola into the real world with free campaign files and maker drops.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="contrib-product-rail" aria-label="Poola spread the word products" data-reveal>
      <article class="contrib-product-card contrib-product-card--wide">
        <div class="shop-preview shop-preview--stand" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><span></span></div>
        <div class="contrib-product-card__body">
          <span>3D print file</span>
          <h3>Pool display stand</h3>
          <p>A small tabletop stand for QR cards, campaign signs and event booths.</p>
          <button class="btn btn--primary" type="button" data-shop-action="Pool display stand">Preview file</button>
        </div>
      </article>
      <article class="contrib-product-card">
        <div class="shop-preview shop-preview--poster" aria-hidden="true"><span>POOL STARTED</span></div>
        <div class="contrib-product-card__body">
          <span>Poster design</span>
          <h3>Window poster kit</h3>
          <p>Printable posters for cafes, studios, libraries and noticeboards.</p>
          <button class="btn btn--ghost" type="button" data-shop-action="Window poster kit">Preview file</button>
        </div>
      </article>
      <article class="contrib-product-card">
        <div class="shop-preview shop-preview--shirt" aria-hidden="true"><i class="fa-solid fa-shirt"></i><span>People Power</span></div>
        <div class="contrib-product-card__body">
          <span>Clothing graphic</span>
          <h3>People Power tee mark</h3>
          <p>Artwork for screen printing, transfers and local merch runs.</p>
          <button class="btn btn--ghost" type="button" data-shop-action="People Power tee mark">Request drop</button>
        </div>
      </article>
      <article class="contrib-product-card">
        <div class="shop-preview shop-preview--stickers" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><span></span></div>
        <div class="contrib-product-card__body">
          <span>Sticker sheet</span>
          <h3>Support signal stickers</h3>
          <p>Small labels for laptops, packages, community boards and maker tables.</p>
          <button class="btn btn--ghost" type="button" data-shop-action="Support signal stickers">Preview file</button>
        </div>
      </article>
      <article class="contrib-product-card">
        <div class="shop-preview shop-preview--badge" aria-hidden="true"><span>BACKER</span></div>
        <div class="contrib-product-card__body">
          <span>Badge template</span>
          <h3>Backer badge set</h3>
          <p>Printable badges for launches, meetups and local campaign days.</p>
          <button class="btn btn--ghost" type="button" data-shop-action="Backer badge set">Request drop</button>
        </div>
      </article>
      <article class="contrib-product-card">
        <div class="shop-preview shop-preview--kit" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><span></span></div>
        <div class="contrib-product-card__body">
          <span>Campaign kit</span>
          <h3>Community table kit</h3>
          <p>A printable field kit for explaining a Pool at schools, markets and events.</p>
          <button class="btn btn--ghost" type="button" data-shop-action="Community table kit">Coming soon</button>
        </div>
      </article>
    </div>
    <p class="shop-status container" data-shop-status aria-live="polite"></p>
  </section>

  <section class="section contrib-founder-note">
    <div class="container founder-open-note" data-reveal>
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Founder note</p>
        <h2>This is not a large-team claim.</h2>
      </div>
      <p>Poola is currently founder-led. The contributor story is a direction: build enough in public that useful people can help without needing private context, while keeping the parts that affect trust, money and safety responsibly controlled.</p>
      <div class="policy-meta">
        <span>Founder-led today</span>
        <span>Contributor-ready by design</span>
        <span>Selective open-source scope</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section final-cta contrib-cta">
    <div class="container final-cta__inner" data-reveal>
      <p class="signal"><span></span> Build with Poola</p>
      <h2>Useful contributors can shape the trust layer early.</h2>
      <p>Engineering, design, safety, local pilots, campaign templates and AI workflows are all meaningful places to help.</p>
      <div class="cta-actions">
        <a class="btn btn--primary" href="contact.html" data-magnetic>Contact Poola</a>
        <a class="btn btn--ghost btn--on-dark" href="features.html">Product map</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <style>
    @media (min-width: 821px) {
      :global(html.contributors-shell) {
        background-color: #071113;
        background-image: none;
      }

      :global(html.contributors-shell.no-native-page-transitions) {
        animation: contributorsShellBlackIn 760ms var(--ease) both;
      }

      :global(html.contributors-shell.is-shell-exiting) {
        animation: contributorsShellBlackOut 460ms var(--ease) both;
      }

      @keyframes contributorsShellBlackIn {
        0% {
          background-color: var(--shell-bg);
        }

        100% {
          background-color: #071113;
        }
      }

      @keyframes contributorsShellBlackOut {
        0% {
          background-color: #071113;
        }

        100% {
          background-color: var(--shell-bg);
        }
      }
    }

    @media (min-width: 821px) and (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
      :global(html.contributors-shell),
      :global(html.contributors-shell.no-native-page-transitions),
      :global(html.contributors-shell.is-shell-exiting) {
        animation: none;
      }
    }

    .contrib-hero {
      position: relative;
      overflow: hidden;
      min-height: calc(100svh - var(--nav-h));
      color: var(--ink);
      background:
        radial-gradient(680px 420px at 78% 30%, rgba(121, 214, 220, 0.24), transparent 62%),
        radial-gradient(620px 420px at 18% 16%, rgba(255, 159, 64, 0.14), transparent 58%),
        linear-gradient(180deg, #f8fbff 0%, #ffffff 74%);
    }

    .contrib-hero::before {
      content: "";
      position: absolute;
      inset: 0;
      pointer-events: none;
      opacity: 0.62;
      background-image:
        linear-gradient(rgba(7, 17, 19, 0.07) 1px, transparent 1px),
        linear-gradient(90deg, rgba(7, 17, 19, 0.07) 1px, transparent 1px);
      background-size: 42px 42px;
      mask-image: linear-gradient(180deg, black, transparent 82%);
    }

    .contrib-hero__grid {
      position: relative;
      min-height: calc(100svh - var(--nav-h));
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 0.92fr) minmax(360px, 520px);
      gap: 70px;
      align-items: center;
      padding-block: 88px 74px;
    }

    .contrib-hero .signal,
    .contrib-hero .hero__sub,
    .contrib-hero .btn--ghost {
      color: var(--muted);
    }

    .contrib-hero h1 {
      max-width: 10.8ch;
      margin-bottom: 26px;
      color: var(--ink);
    }

    .contrib-console {
      border: 1px solid rgba(7, 17, 19, 0.12);
      border-radius: 18px;
      overflow: hidden;
      background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.78);
      box-shadow: var(--shadow), inset 0 1px rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.88);
      backdrop-filter: blur(24px) saturate(130%);
      -webkit-backdrop-filter: blur(24px) saturate(130%);
    }

    .contrib-console__bar {
      display: flex;
      align-items: center;
      gap: 8px;
      min-height: 46px;
      padding: 0 16px;
      border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(7, 17, 19, 0.1);
      color: rgba(7, 17, 19, 0.58);
      font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, Monaco, Consolas, "Liberation Mono", monospace;
      font-size: 0.8rem;
    }

    .contrib-console__bar span {
      width: 10px;
      height: 10px;
      border-radius: 50%;
      background: var(--pink);
    }

    .contrib-console__bar span:nth-child(2) {
      background: var(--sun);
    }

    .contrib-console__bar span:nth-child(3) {
      background: var(--aqua);
    }

    .contrib-console__bar strong {
      margin-left: 8px;
      font-weight: 700;
    }

    .contrib-console__body {
      display: grid;
      gap: 20px;
      padding: 24px;
    }

    .contrib-command {
      display: flex;
      gap: 12px;
      align-items: center;
      min-height: 52px;
      padding: 0 14px;
      border: 1px solid rgba(7, 17, 19, 0.1);
      border-radius: 10px;
      background: rgba(248, 251, 255, 0.88);
      color: var(--ink);
      font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, Monaco, Consolas, "Liberation Mono", monospace;
      font-size: 0.88rem;
    }

    .contrib-command span {
      color: var(--aqua);
      font-weight: 800;
    }

    .contrib-pulse {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: auto 1fr auto 1fr auto;
      gap: 10px;
      align-items: center;
      color: var(--ink-2);
      font-family: var(--font-display);
      font-size: 0.82rem;
      font-weight: 800;
      text-transform: uppercase;
    }

    .contrib-pulse i {
      height: 1px;
      background: linear-gradient(90deg, rgba(121, 214, 220, 0.7), transparent);
    }

    .contrib-queue {
      display: grid;
      gap: 10px;
    }

    .contrib-queue article {
      display: grid;
      gap: 6px;
      padding: 16px;
      border: 1px solid rgba(7, 17, 19, 0.1);
      border-radius: 12px;
      background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.72);
    }

    .contrib-queue span,
    .contrib-track em,
    .artifact-grid b,
    .boundary-board span,
    .pathway-line span {
      color: var(--aqua);
      font-size: 0.72rem;
      font-style: normal;
      font-weight: 850;
      letter-spacing: 0;
      text-transform: uppercase;
    }

    .contrib-queue strong {
      color: var(--ink);
      font-family: var(--font-display);
      font-size: 1.1rem;
      line-height: 1.1;
    }

    .contrib-principles {
      border-block: 1px solid var(--line);
      background: var(--white);
    }

    .contrib-principles__inner {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: repeat(4, minmax(0, 1fr));
      gap: 10px;
    }

    .contrib-principles span {
      min-height: 70px;
      display: grid;
      place-items: center;
      padding: 12px;
      border: 1px solid var(--line);
      border-radius: var(--radius);
      background: var(--mist);
      color: var(--ink);
      font-family: var(--font-display);
      font-weight: 800;
      text-align: center;
      line-height: 1.25;
    }

    .contrib-workboard {
      background: linear-gradient(180deg, #ffffff 0%, #f7fbfb 100%);
    }

    .contrib-workboard__grid,
    .contrib-boundaries__grid {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 0.75fr) minmax(0, 1.25fr);
      gap: 54px;
      align-items: start;
    }

    .contrib-section-copy {
      position: sticky;
      top: calc(var(--nav-h) + 46px);
    }

    .contrib-section-copy h2 {
      max-width: 10ch;
      margin-bottom: 18px;
    }

    .contrib-track-stack {
      display: grid;
      gap: 12px;
    }

    .contrib-track {
      border: 1px solid var(--line);
      border-radius: 14px;
      background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.88);
      box-shadow: var(--shadow-soft);
      overflow: hidden;
    }

    .contrib-track summary {
      min-height: 82px;
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: 46px minmax(0, 1fr) auto;
      gap: 16px;
      align-items: center;
      padding: 0 20px;
      cursor: pointer;
      list-style: none;
    }

    .contrib-track summary::-webkit-details-marker {
      display: none;
    }

    .contrib-track summary span {
      width: 42px;
      height: 42px;
      display: grid;
      place-items: center;
      border-radius: 50%;
      color: var(--white);
      background: var(--ink);
      font-family: var(--font-display);
      font-weight: 850;
      font-size: 0.82rem;
    }

    .contrib-track summary strong {
      font-family: var(--font-display);
      font-size: 1.22rem;
      line-height: 1.1;
    }

    .contrib-track p {
      padding: 0 22px 22px 82px;
      color: var(--muted);
      line-height: 1.65;
    }

    .contrib-artifacts {
      background:
        radial-gradient(760px 340px at 8% 10%, rgba(121, 214, 220, 0.16), transparent 62%),
        var(--white);
    }

    .artifact-grid {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: repeat(6, minmax(0, 1fr));
      gap: 12px;
    }

    .artifact-grid article {
      min-height: 280px;
      display: grid;
      align-content: space-between;
      gap: 16px;
      padding: 20px;
      border: 1px solid var(--line);
      border-radius: 16px;
      background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.9);
      box-shadow: var(--shadow-soft);
    }

    .artifact-grid article:nth-child(1),
    .artifact-grid article:nth-child(4) {
      transform: translateY(24px);
    }

    .artifact-grid span {
      color: var(--teal);
      font-family: var(--font-display);
      font-size: 0.8rem;
      font-weight: 850;
    }

    .artifact-grid h3 {
      margin-top: 28px;
      font-size: 1.34rem;
    }

    .artifact-grid p {
      color: var(--muted);
      font-size: 0.96rem;
      line-height: 1.55;
    }

    .artifact-grid b {
      width: max-content;
      max-width: 100%;
      padding: 7px 10px;
      border-radius: 999px;
      background: var(--foam);
      color: var(--teal-dark);
    }

    .contrib-boundaries {
      color: var(--ink);
      background:
        radial-gradient(620px 320px at 84% 20%, rgba(121, 214, 220, 0.22), transparent 64%),
        radial-gradient(520px 280px at 14% 18%, rgba(255, 159, 64, 0.1), transparent 58%),
        linear-gradient(180deg, #ffffff 0%, #f8fbff 100%);
    }

    .contrib-boundaries .eyebrow,
    .contrib-boundaries h2,
    .contrib-boundaries .lead {
      color: var(--ink);
    }

    .contrib-boundaries .lead {
      color: var(--muted);
    }

    .boundary-board {
      display: grid;
      gap: 12px;
    }

    .boundary-board article {
      display: grid;
      gap: 10px;
      padding: 24px;
      border: 1px solid var(--line);
      border-radius: 16px;
      background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.86);
      box-shadow: var(--shadow-soft);
    }

    .boundary-board article:nth-child(2) {
      margin-left: 34px;
    }

    .boundary-board article:nth-child(3) {
      margin-left: 68px;
    }

    .boundary-board h3 {
      color: var(--ink);
      font-size: 1.35rem;
    }

    .boundary-board p {
      color: var(--muted);
    }

    .contrib-pathway {
      background: linear-gradient(180deg, #ffffff 0%, #f8fbff 100%);
    }

    .pathway-line {
      position: relative;
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: repeat(4, minmax(0, 1fr));
      gap: 14px;
    }

    .pathway-line::before {
      content: "";
      position: absolute;
      top: 31px;
      left: var(--gutter);
      right: var(--gutter);
      height: 2px;
      background: linear-gradient(90deg, var(--teal), var(--aqua), var(--sun));
    }

    .pathway-line article {
      position: relative;
